WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.035
-I want to ask this -- You know,
and, again,

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:04.938
we can't talk about when you
and your colleagues talk about

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:06.773 size:78% position:39%
cases that are before
the Supreme Court.

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think one thing that's
fascinating to

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
people like myself who don't
understand the workings

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:13.847
of the court -- what do yo
talk about when you're on break?

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:15.315 line:92%
What do you talk about --

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:17.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it true that
you have lunch together?

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:22.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
-After every argument and afte
every conference on Friday

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:25.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what do other people
talk about

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:27.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
when they're not talking
about business?

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:30.163 line:92%
The movies, books, the family,

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:36.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
whose child is behaving
and who child is misbehaving

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.271 line:92%
We talk like anyone else.

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:40.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When you talk about movies,
is it always that

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:43.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
five people like it
and four don't?

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:49.382
Do you ever -- Are there eve
unanimous opinions on movies

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:52.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, for a different reason,
there isn't.

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are some people
on the court

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.056 line:92%
who don't really look at movies.

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:56.589 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, right.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.558 size:75% position:38%
-And there are other
people on the court,

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:01.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
like one of my colleagues
who speaks French --

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:04.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, when he's seen a
French movie, I can't watch it

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
and tell him whether I
like it or not.

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:07.000 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I see.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.770 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-So --- But, no, not --

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.139
Thankfully, not all of us
watch the same movies.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:13.706 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's good.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's probably,
I would say, for the best.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.378 size:88% position:44% line:92%
You -- Ask really quick.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:21.781 size:81% position:41%
You know, obviously,
Ruth Bader Ginsburg --

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:22.348 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
an iconic figure.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:24.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
She had some
health scares this year.

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:25.652 line:92%
She is back. How's she doing

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:29.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
And is it -- Is she
a good colleague to have?

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:31.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She's a wonderful
colleague to have.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:36.396 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:41.034
Every step of the way, for me,
that I've been on the court,

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:43.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
Justice Ginsburg
has been there to welcome me

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
from my very first day there
where she lent me --

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:50.910
or gave me -- a copy of he
bench manual that tells yo

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
how she runs her chambers
so I didn't have to

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:57.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
start from scratch, to the tim
I issued my first opinion

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:02.922
and she sent me a note telling
me what a fine opinion it was,

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:09.162
to everything else that she does
to help my life

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.196 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
there on the court.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:15.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she's an amazing, brave,
woman -- and strong.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:20.340
I call her "The Steel Magnolia."
-Oh, that's very nice.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:27.380
-Delicate on the outside, bu
she has an iron rod behind her

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, thank you so much
for being here.

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:29.649 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:32.385
-And I wish the best to yo
and all your colleagues.

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:32.919 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:36.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And this is Justice
Sonia Sotomayor, everybody

